# Architecture

This is not a modular monolith, MVC app, or clean-architecture template. Do not impose those layers.

## What exists

- `mobile/` — Expo SDK 54 + Expo Router 6 (file routes under `mobile/app/`). Mock auth. Placeholder Home/Profile/Settings. No domain screens.
- `backend/` — Express 5 CommonJS declared in `package.json`. No server entry file, no routes, no database client.
- No `supabase/` directory. No web frontend.

## What must not happen without an approved ADR

- Replacing Expo with a web app (engineering pack called mobile out of scope; the repo is mobile — keep Expo). See `documentation/decisions/ADR-0005-expo-mobile-vs-web-pack.md`.
- Migrating backend to TypeScript or adding Nest/Fastify/ORMs. See ADR-0001.
- Introducing leave-balance, overtime, payroll, SSO, Teams/Slack, or multi-tenant `org_id`.
- Manager-in-app leave approval (Confirmed: approval is outside the app). See ADR-0004.

## Proposed target (unsigned)

Express API `/api/v1` → Supabase Auth + PostgreSQL + Storage. Modules named in the pack (`auth`, `employees`, `leave`, `attendance`, `calendar`, `documents`, `notifications`, `reports`, `audit`, `config`) are a blueprint, not existing folders.

When adding backend code, start from Express in `backend/` without extra frameworks. Put domain rules on the server.
